# fifo_frame_wrap: Commands straddling the ring's end (one page, start 0x400: a ring of 0x3c00 bytes) are read across it: a header split 6 + 6; a DefineChildFIFO whose 4-byte id is split 1 + 3 (the page after the ring holds 0xff, so a read past the end would name no valid FIFO); a barrier whose index is split 2 + 2 (0xff bytes would make it out of range); and a faulting command whose header starts 8 bytes before the end, whose fault offset (0x103c) is that ring offset, not the free-running count.
